    {
      "text": "Revenue conflict: news report S1 states revenue rose to ₹1,428 crore, a 35% increase, while the official filing S3 reports revenue of ₹1,248 crore, an 18.0% YoY increase for the quarter ended 30 June 2026.",
      "citations": ["S1","S3"],
      "evidence": [{"id":"S1:E2"},{"id":"S3:E3"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "Historical pledge comparison: a 2024 news article reported promoters pledged 35% of their holding, whereas the June 2026 shareholding pattern shows pledged 4.1% of promoter holding.",
